  "distinctions_and_findings": [
    "C independent chord layer uses rests for rhythmic entry; F/H added stems/beams can point out melodic layers and do not imply one universal rest policy.",
    "Visible dotted-eighth164 at E reconfirmed; equivalent quarter123/dotted-quarter82 are arithmetic, not measured playback. m92 equation direction stays unresolved.",
    "Ordinary sixteenths and triplet eighths in m186-189 share beat boundaries, not ordinal note alignment; resting fast slots and held slow notes differ.",
    "J foreground: half-rest first, lower eighth pair beat3 then upper pair beat4. Low octave has visible ties across12/8 to C transition.",
    "Tempo/accompaniment preparation at20 precedes A24; accelerando162 precedes K164. Stage boundaries cannot be collapsed for visual alignment.",
    "Capacity changes with metre, layer and densest activity. Two-to-six bars per system are descriptions, not a recommended template.",
    "Solid cross-staff voice guides differ from glissandi; Gould prefers dotted guides, a conditional style candidate rather than automatic replacement.",
    "Ending201 has whole-bar rests with fermatas; not automatically transferred to previous sounding chord or an assertion about pedal release."
